<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rohilkhand</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rohilkhand is a region of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bareilly">Bareilly</a>, Moradabad and Rampur. It is named after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rohillas">Rohilla Afghans</a> who settled and ruled it in the 18th century. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rohilla-war">Rohilla War</a> of 1774 most of it went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Awadh</a>, and in 1801 it was ceded to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rohilkhand.jpg" alt="Rohilkhand" width="320" height="266" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sita Ram · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_mausoleum_of_Hafiz_Rahmat_Khan_at_Bareilly,_1814-15.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
